## Signal ID: Friction-2026-10-23-Frontline-Authentication-Friction
Type: Friction
What Changed: Organizations with frontline workers (healthcare, manufacturing) paying for authentication/access systems still experience high interruption rates, leading to productivity loss and security workarounds. Report published mid-Oct 2026.
Friction: Authentication / Cross-device / Support - Shared devices, MFA prompts, password resets, connectivity causing repeated interruptions for frontline staff.
Money: Organizations already invest in identity/auth solutions, yet workers lose ~2.5 hours/month each (affected), totaling ~32,400 hours/year for average 2,800-worker org. Workarounds (sharing credentials, staying logged in) create risk/compliance costs. Delays impact production/patient care (revenue/operational).
Evidence:
1. Imprivata + FIDO Alliance report "Frontline Friction" (survey Aug 2026, published ~2026-10-19): 37% frontline workers experience auth issue monthly; ~11 interruptions, 2.5h lost each; 95% orgs observe workarounds (40% stay logged in, 36% bypass MFA, 33% share credentials); only 40% confident in attribution. Average org loses 32,400 working hours annually. URL: https://fidoalliance.org/authentication-issues-cost-frontline-organizations-thousands-of-working-hours-each-year-according-to-research-from-imprivata-and-fido-alliance/
2. Multiple coverage (Biometric Update, Security Magazine, etc., 2026-10-19 to 2026-10-22) confirming numbers and workarounds.
Mechanism: Auth friction in shared/high-tempo environments forces manual interruptions or insecure workarounds, converting paid security controls into labor waste and residual risk. Inference: current password/MFA implementations poorly matched to frontline workflows.
Current Workaround: Staying logged in, credential sharing, MFA bypass attempts. Cost: lost productive hours + security/accountability gaps (evidenced by survey).
Payer: Frontline-intensive organizations / their IT/security teams (already paying for better auth solutions like Imprivata; passwordless adoption partial).
Economic Effect: labor cost / time loss / potential operational revenue delay / compliance risk
Friction Value: Frequency high (37% workers monthly, multiple interruptions); per-event ~minutes of lost time aggregating to 2.5h/worker/month; recoverable via better passwordless/shared-device auth (survey notes benefits for adopters). Based on survey estimates; monetary conversion of hours unknown.
Persistence: Structural (shared devices, protective equipment, workflow constraints ongoing)
Next Question: What is the willingness-to-pay or current spend on specialized frontline auth solutions vs residual hours lost, and adoption barriers for passwordless?
